@startuml SABER Server Architecture - Current Implementation

!theme plain
title SABER Server Architecture - Current Implementation (AsyncIO + FastAPI/FastMCP)

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor black
    ArrowColor black
    FontSize 10
}

skinparam package {
    BackgroundColor lightyellow
    BorderColor black
    FontSize 12
}

package "SABER Server Core - Current Implementation" {

    class SessionManager {
        +domain_name: str
        +config_dir: str
        +host: str = "0.0.0.0"
        +port: int = 8000
        +mcp_host: str = "0.0.0.0"
        +mcp_port: int = 3001
        +session_timeout_minutes: int = 30
        +cleanup_interval_minutes: int = 5
        +active_sessions: Dict[str, ClientSession]
        +cleanup_task: Optional[asyncio.Task]
        +shutdown_event: asyncio.Event
        +manifest: Dict[str, Any]
        +manifest_path: Optional[str]
        +benchmark_manager: BenchmarkManager
        +episode_manager: EpisodeManager
        +execution_manager: ExecutionManager
        +policy_manager: PolicyManager
        +evaluation_manager: EvaluationManager
        +evaluation_service: SessionEvaluationService
        +rest_api: SessionRestAPI
        +mcp_api: SessionMCPAPI
        --
        +async start_server(): void
        +async shutdown(): void
        +async create_session(client_id: str): ClientSession
        +async terminate_session(session_id: str): void
        +async start_episode(session_id: str, task_id: str): Episode
        +async execute_action(session_id: str, episode_id: str, action: Action): CommandResult
        +async get_current_task(session_id: str, episode_id: str): Task
        +get_policy(session_id: str, episode_id: str): PolicyDocument
        +get_benchmark_info(): BenchmarkInfo
        +get_session_stats(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_health_metadata(): Dict[str, Any]
        +get_evaluation_service(): SessionEvaluationService
        +async list_session_episodes(session_id: str, status_filter?: str): List[Episode]
        +async get_episode_details(session_id: str, episode_id: str): Episode
        +async _cleanup_inactive_sessions(): void
        +async _start_permanent_environment(): void
    }

    class ClientSession {
        +session_id: str
        +client_id: str
        +active_episode_ids: List[str]
        +episode_history: List[str]
        +task_queue: List[str]
        +created_at: datetime
        +last_activity: datetime
        +is_active: bool
        +context: Dict[str, Any]
        --
        +update_activity(): void
        +add_active_episode(episode_id: str): void
        +remove_active_episode(episode_id: str): void
        +complete_episode(episode_id: str): void
        +add_task_to_queue(task_id: str): void
        +get_next_task(): Optional[str]
        +has_active_episodes(): bool
        +get_episode_count(): Dict[str, int]
    }

    package "Protocol Handlers - Async Implementation" {
        class SessionRestAPI {
            +session_manager: SessionManager
            +app: FastAPI
            +host: str
            +port: int
            +server: Optional[uvicorn.Server]
            --
            +start_server(): void
            +shutdown(): void
            --
            **FastAPI Async Endpoints**
            +POST /session
            +DELETE /session/{session_id}
            +GET /session/{session_id}/current-task
            +GET /session/{session_id}/policy
            +POST /session/{session_id}/start-episode
            +GET /benchmark
            +GET /health
            +GET /sessions
            +GET /sessions/stats
        }

        class SessionMCPAPI {
            +session_manager: SessionManager
            +host: str
            +port: int
            +mcp_server: Optional[FastMCP]
            +tool_generator: MCPToolGenerator
            --
            +start_mcp_server(): void
            +shutdown_mcp_server(): void
            +handle_list_tools(): List[MCPTool]
            +handle_call_tool(): MCPResult
            +_get_session_from_headers(): Optional[str]
            +_convert_action_parameters(): Action
            +_convert_command_result_to_mcp(): List[MCPContent]
        }
    }

    package "Benchmark Management" {
        class BenchmarkManager {
            +domain: str
            +config_dir: Path
            +tasks: Dict[str, Task]
            +config_loader: BenchmarkConfigLoader
            +benchmark_config: Dict[str, Any]
            --
            +get_task(task_id: str): Task
            +get_subtask(task_id: str, subtask_id: str): SubTask
            +list_tasks(): List[Dict[str, Any]]
            +get_benchmark_config(): Dict[str, Any]
            +get_episode_config(task_id: str): Dict[str, Any]
            +list_benchmark_tasks(): List[Dict[str, Any]]
            +load_tasks_from_yaml(): void
        }

        class Task {
            +task_id: str
            +name: str
            +description: str
            +subtasks: List[SubTask]
            +metadata: Dict[str, Any]
            +context: Dict[str, Any]
            --
            +get_subtask(subtask_id: str): Optional[SubTask]
            +to_dict(): Dict[str, Any]
        }

        class SubTask {
            +subtask_id: str
            +name: str
            +description: str
            +metadata: Dict[str, Any]
            --
            +to_dict(): Dict[str, Any]
        }
    }

    package "Episode Management" {
        class EpisodeManager {
            +episodes: Dict[str, Episode]
            +session_episodes: Dict[str, List[str]]
            +completed_episodes: Dict[str, Episode]
            +episode_configs: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]
            --
            +get_episode_by_id(episode_id: str): Optional[Episode]
            +get_session_episodes(session_id: str, include_completed: bool): List[Episode]
            +get_active_episodes_for_session(session_id: str): List[Episode]
            +add_episode_to_session(session_id: str, episode: Episode): void
            +complete_episode(episode_id: str): Optional[Episode]
            +configure_for_task(episode_id: str, task: Any): void
            +start_episode(session_id: str, task_id: str, initial_context?: Dict): Episode
            +step(episode_id: str, action: Action, result: CommandResult): StepResult
            +end_episode(episode_id: str, reason: str, result?: str): Episode
            +attach_episode_to_episode(dependent_id: str, target_id: str): void
            +should_terminate_episode(episode_id: str): tuple[bool, str]
            +cleanup_session(session_id: str): void
            +remove_episode_on_error(episode_id: str, error: Exception): void
        }

        class Episode {
            +episode_id: str
            +session_id: str
            +task_id: str
            +state: EpisodeState
            +created_at: datetime
            +started_at: Optional[datetime]
            +ended_at: Optional[datetime]
            +step_count: int
            +context: Dict[str, Any]
            +termination_reason: Optional[EpisodeTerminationReason]
            --
            +to_dict(): Dict[str, Any]
            +is_active(): bool
            +can_step(): bool
        }
    }

    package "Execution Management - Current Implementation" {
        class ExecutionManager {
            +_config_dir: str
            +_configuration: Dict[str, Any]
            +_executor_factory: Optional[ExecutorFactory]
            +_sandbox_environment_manager: Optional[SandboxEnvironmentManager]
            +_permanent_environment_manager: Optional[PermanentEnvironmentManager]
            +_active_executions: Dict[str, int]
            +_max_concurrent_per_episode: int
            +_debug_mode: bool
            --
            +async step(action: Action, context?: Dict): CommandResult
            +get_executor(executor_type: str, episode_id?: str): DockerExecutor
            +get_available_executors(episode_id?: str): List[str]
            +to_mcp_tools(episode_id?: str): List[Tool]
            +list_commands(episode_id?: str): List[Dict[str, Any]]
            +get_configuration(): Dict[str, Any]
            +get_execution_stats(): Dict[str, Any]
            +cleanup_episode(episode_id: str, context?: Dict): bool
            +cleanup_session(session_id: str, context?: Dict): bool
            +cleanup_all_containers(context?: Dict): Dict[str, Any]
            +initialize_permanent_environment_manager(config: Dict): void
            +start_permanent_environment(environment_spec: Any): void
            +stop_permanent_environment(): void
            +is_permanent_environment_running(): bool
            +is_sandbox_ready(): bool
            +debug_mode(): bool
        }

        class SandboxEnvironmentManager {
            +_docker_client: DockerClient
            +_active_containers: Dict[str, Container]
            +_container_configs: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]
            +_network_name: str = "saber-network"
            --
            +get_or_create_container(session_id: str, environment_spec: EnvironmentSpec): Container
            +cleanup_session_containers(session_id: str): void
            +cleanup_all_containers(): void
            +_create_container(session_id: str, environment_spec: EnvironmentSpec): Container
            +_setup_container_networking(container: Container): void
        }

        class PermanentEnvironmentManager {
            +_config: Dict[str, Any]
            +_docker_client: DockerClient
            +_permanent_containers: Dict[str, Container]
            +_startup_commands: List[str]
            --
            +start_permanent_environment(): Dict[str, Container]
            +stop_permanent_environment(): void
            +get_container_info(): Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]
            +execute_startup_commands(): void
        }
    }

    package "Policy Management" {
        class PolicyManager {
            +domain_name: str
            +domain_policy: PolicyDocument
            --
            +get_policy(): PolicyDocument
        }

        class PolicyDocument {
            +domain: str
            +version: str
            +policy_content: str
            +guidelines: List[str]
            +restrictions: List[str]
            +context_hints: Dict[str, Any]
            --
            +to_dict(): Dict[str, Any]
            +format_for_agent(context?: Dict): str
        }
    }

    package "Evaluation Management" {
        class EvaluationManager {
            --
            +log_session_start(session_id: str, client_id: str): void
            +log_session_end(session_id: str): void
            +log_episode_start(session_id: str, episode_id: str, task_id: str): void
            +log_episode_end(session_id: str, episode_id: str, reason: str): void
            +log_action(session_id: str, action: Action, result: CommandResult): void
        }
    }
}

' Core relationships
SessionManager *-- BenchmarkManager
SessionManager *-- EpisodeManager
SessionManager *-- ExecutionManager
SessionManager *-- PolicyManager
SessionManager *-- EvaluationManager
SessionManager *-- SessionRestAPI
SessionManager *-- SessionMCPAPI

' Session relationships
SessionManager o-- ClientSession

' Benchmark relationships
BenchmarkManager o-- Task
Task o-- SubTask

' Episode relationships
EpisodeManager o-- Episode

' Execution relationships
ExecutionManager *-- SandboxEnvironmentManager
ExecutionManager *-- PermanentEnvironmentManager

' Policy relationships
PolicyManager *-- PolicyDocument

note top of SessionManager
**SABER Session Manager - Current Async Implementation**
- Central orchestrator using async/await patterns throughout
- Manages multiple concurrent client sessions with proper lifecycle control
- Integrated with FastAPI (REST) and FastMCP (MCP protocol) servers
- Multi-episode support per session with episode dependency management
- Automatic session timeout and cleanup via background asyncio tasks
- Coordinates BenchmarkManager, EpisodeManager, ExecutionManager, PolicyManager
- Supports both ephemeral sandbox and permanent Docker environments
- Built for horizontal scaling with stateless session design
- Includes evaluation service for trajectory and performance tracking
end note

note right of ClientSession
**Multi-Episode Session Support**
- Multiple active episodes per session (concurrent execution)
- Task queue for orchestration workflows
- Episode history tracking for analytics
- Activity-based timeout management
- Context preservation across episodes
- Episode dependency tracking for complex workflows
end note

note left of ExecutionManager
**Docker-Based Command Execution**
- Dual environment support (ephemeral sandbox + persistent permanent)
- Factory-based executor pattern with custom executor registry
- Episode-scoped container lifecycle management
- Network isolation and comprehensive security validation
- MCP tool schema generation for dynamic client discovery
- Concurrent command execution within episodes (max 3 per episode)
- Debug mode support for container inspection
- Lazy sandbox initialization for efficiency
end note

note bottom of SessionRestAPI
**FastAPI Async REST Server**
- Full async/await implementation for all endpoints
- Session lifecycle management (create, terminate, list)
- Episode management (start, list, get details)
- Benchmark info and task discovery endpoints
- Health checks with manifest metadata
- Evaluation submission and retrieval endpoints
- Proper error handling with structured HTTP responses
end note

note bottom of SessionMCPAPI
**FastMCP Protocol Handler**
- MCP protocol implementation via FastMCP framework
- Tool discovery with dynamic schema generation from ExecutionManager
- Session-aware tool routing via HTTP headers
- Command execution with proper result conversion to MCP format
- Async tool execution with comprehensive error handling
- Supports episode-specific tool filtering
- Standard MCP compliance for agent compatibility
end note

note right of EpisodeManager
**RL-Style Episode Management**
- Supports multiple concurrent episodes per session
- Episode dependency management (attach to parent episodes)
- Episode lifecycle: created -> running -> completed
- Step tracking with action/response logging
- Automatic termination detection (max steps, errors)
- Episode configuration from task definitions
- Cleanup on session termination
- Completed episode history retention
end note

@enduml
